{{also|Dinger}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|ding|er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪŋ(ɡ)ə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 dinger.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[bell]] or [[chime]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Sarah Gregory|title=Public Trust|page=47|publisher=Signet|year_published=1997|isbn=9780451190765
|passage=Sharon patted the '''dinger''' to call for service.}}
# The suspended [[clapper]] of a [[bell]].
# One who rings a bell.
# {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[home run]].
#: ''The starting pitcher gave up three '''dingers'''.''
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1989|author=John Holway|title=Strikeouts: The High Cost of Hitting Home Runs|titleurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=ETQDAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA24|journal=Baseball Digest|month=June
|passage=He should know, he fanned 2597 times — far more than any other man — but made millions hitting 563 '''dingers'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Hank Davis|title=Small-Town Heroes: Images of Minor League Baseball|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=0T6QCyo7qrwC&pg=PA264|page=264|publisher=University of Nebraska Press|year_published=2003|isbn=0803266391
|passage=Then as you're taking his picture, say something about the thirty '''dingers''' he's going to hit this season. You get that little extra smile on his face.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=[[w:Mike Stone (radio personality)|Mike Stone]]|author2=[[w:Art Regner|Art Regner]]|title=The Great Book of Detroit Sports Lists|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=aceROmDTQsoC&pg=PA209|page=209|publisher=Running Press|year_published=2008|isbn=9780762433544
|passage=For you youngsters out there, hitting 50 '''dingers''' in the pre-steroid craze days of the early 90s was an actual accomplishment; the only questionable substance Fielder was putting in his body were McRib sandwiches.}}
# {{lb|en|North America|slang}} The [[penis]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:penis}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=Max Evans|title=Bluefeather Fellini in the Sacred Realm|page=131|publisher=University Press of Colorado|year_published=1994|isbn=9780553565409
|passage="He had a red wool sock on his '''dinger'''. That's all."}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang}} Something [[outstanding]] or [[exceptional]], a [[humdinger]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1932|year_published=1965|author=Delos W. Lovelace|authorlink=Delos W. Lovelace|title=[[w:King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong]]|page=21|passage=‘Say, does that sock in the jaw hurt any more? It was a '''dinger'''.’}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1939|author={{w|John Steinbeck}}|title={{w|The Grapes of Wrath}}|url=https://archive.org/details/grapesofwrath1976stei|chapter=4|page=28|publisher=Penguin|year_published=1951
|passage=Casy said, “See how good the corn come along until the dust got up. Been a '''dinger''' of a crop.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author={{w|Earl Emerson}}|title=Catfish Café|location=New York|publisher=Ballantine|chapter=1|page=3|url=https://archive.org/details/catfishcafe00emer
|passage=“I won’t lie to you. She been in trouble the last couple years, but she got herself wrapped up in a real '''dinger''' this time.”}}
# {{lb|en|Australian slang|}} A [[condom]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:condom}}
# {{lb|en|Australian slang}} The [[buttocks]], the [[anus]].
#: {{syn|en|ding}}
#: ''Let′s leave them to sit on their '''dingers''' for a while.''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1955|author=Norman Bartlett|title=Island Victory|publisher=Angus and Robertson|year_published=1955|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=jVFEAAAAIAAJ&q=%22on+their+dingers%22|page=6
|passage="We'd get even more out of 'em if some of the pilots sat on their '''dingers''' less and polished their kites more."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1979|author=Derek Maitland|title=Breaking Out|publisher=Allen Lane|year_published=1979|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=Vi9XAAAAYAAJ&q=%22his+dinger%22|page=63
|passage=And why had he belted the Australian envoy flat on his '''dinger''' in that Spanish bar?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Peter Pinney|title=The Barbarians: A Soldier's New Guinea Diary|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=rNtHAAAAYAAJ&q=%22his+dinger%22|page=109|publisher=University of Queensland Press|year_published=1988|isbn=9780702221583
|passage="Yeah? Well, stand up anyone who's got a three-inch mortar hid up his '''dinger'''!"}}
# {{lb|en|Australian slang}} A [[catapult]], a [[shanghai]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=[[w:Gordon Briscoe|Gordon Briscoe]]|title=Racial Folly: A Twentieth-Century Aboriginal Family|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=FH0MenEDMsIC&pg=PA59|page=59|publisher=Anu E Press|year_published=2010|isbn=9781921666209
|passage=We made our ''''dingers'''' (as we called them) out of truck tyre inner tubes that were heavy-duty rubber that could shoot a stone a very long distance.}}
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} An [[unregistered]] [[car]].

